\name{BaseRViolinLayerProcessor}
\alias{BaseRViolinLayerProcessor}
\title{Base R Violin Layer Processor}
\description{
Reads a \code{vioplot::vioplot()} call as the \code{violin_box} + \code{violin_kde} layer
pair, matching what the ggplot2 adapter produces for \code{geom_violin()}. Which
plotting system a user chose should not decide whether their chart is
accessible.

\code{vioplot()} returns its box summary but not the density curve it drew, so
both are recovered by replaying the call vioplot makes internally --- see
\code{\link[=compute_vioplot_stats]{compute_vioplot_stats()}}, which records why that is a transcription rather
than an approximation.
}
\keyword{internal}
